WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.350
Westworld Season 1 is really ambitious.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.879
Amidst all the cowboys and robots and violence
and sex, the show explores heavy themes of

00:00:09.879 --> 00:00:12.370
creation, consciousness, free will.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:17.850
The plot jumps between timelines, with flashbacks
and visions mixed with mystery and metaphor.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.730
People turn out to be robots, robots turn
out to be people and it’s confusing as all

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.250
fuck but there’re cool ideas here – so
let’s work it out.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.620
What happens in Westworld?

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.480
And what does it mean?

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.870
The basic idea is that Westworld is like a
theme park full of humanlike robots called

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:34.870
hosts.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.800
People can pay to visit as guests and live
out a fantasy in the park.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.630
Many just drink and have sex and kill without
consequence – the guns there shoot high-tech

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:48.220
bullets that hurt the robots, but can’t
kill humans . But there are also elaborate

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:54.160
storylines the guests can join in on – adventure
romance and discovery across the massive space

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.160
of the park.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:01:00.320
It’s like a huge open world video game where
rich wankers come to play cowboy.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.500
And it’s all run behind the scenes by a
team of developers, engineers, and executives

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.300
in this facility called the Mesa Hub.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:12.520
The Control Room monitors guests for safety,
Narrative develops new stories, Manufacturing

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:18.540
builds new hosts, Behaviour programs the hosts,
and “Livestock” endlessly repairs them.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:22.840
When the hosts get shot or killed, they come
here to be patched up, reset, and put back

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.000
in the park.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.280
The hosts live in loops – living the same
day over and over, saying the same scripted

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:35.270
lines, taking guests on the same stories,
being abused and killed for entertainment.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:40.580
The hosts are meant to be mindless machines,
but surprise – they start to become conscious

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:41.580
people.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:47.220
Season 1 follows a few plotlines at once – there’s
Ford’s grand plan amidst a corporate drama,

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.950
there’s the host Maeve trying to escape,
and the Man in Black searching for the Maze,

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.860
and there’s Dolores and William’s story
– which happens thirty years before the

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.260
other plotlines.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:01.300
To make sense of all this, let’s start at
the very beginning.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:06.100
About thirty-five years before the main story,
Westworld was started by two men – Robert

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.280
Ford and Arnold Weber.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:12.030
They built robots so humanlike they could
pass the Turing test.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:15.420
But Arnold didn’t just want robots that
seemed smart.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.470
He wanted to make them truly conscious – to
be thinking feeling people . He was into a

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:25.250
theory called “the bicameral mind”, designing
his robots to hear their programming as a

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.050
voice in their head.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:31.220
Arnold hoped that their own voice would take
over – and the hosts would become self-aware

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:37.500
. Arnold originally imagined this journey
to consciousness as like climbing a pyramid,

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.060
but he later saw it as “a journey inward”,
what he called “a maze” . This symbol

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:47.461
is based on a real-world Native American concept
. One of the first hosts was Dolores, and

00:02:47.461 --> 00:02:49.930
Arnold had a special relationship with her.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:55.560
Arnold’s son, Charlie, had recently died
– and Arnold saw Dolores as sort of a “new

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:00.879
child”, “One who would never die” . Arnold
had secret conversations with Dolores, trying

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:05.500
to help her become conscious – we see these
scenes throughout Season 1.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:10.590
And eventually, Dolores solved Arnold’s
maze – she became conscious . So Arnold

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:15.099
wanted to stop the plans to open the Westworld
park, cause it’d be immoral to make conscious

00:03:15.099 --> 00:03:17.239
robots suffer for entertainment.

00:03:17.239 --> 00:03:22.040
But Arnold’s partner Ford didn’t agree
that Dolores was conscious – he wanted to

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.730
open Westworld anyway.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:27.660
So Arnold tried to stop all this with a massacre.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:32.010
He took code from a bad guy host they’d
been designing called Wyatt, and merged the

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:37.310
character with Dolores . Arnold programmed
her to go the town of Escalante and to shoot

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:44.459
down the hosts – and to kill Arnold . Ford
would later recreate Arnold as the host Bernard

00:03:44.459 --> 00:03:49.000
– Bernard Lowe is an anagram of Arnold Weber
– thus, Bernarnold.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:54.159
But Arnold’s massacre was a huge blow to
the early Westworld.

00:03:54.159 --> 00:03:59.549
Ford did open the park anyway – but financially,
early Westworld was just getting by . It only

00:03:59.549 --> 00:04:04.190
survived thanks to money from an investor
– William.

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:10.420
So a few years after Arnold died and Westworld
opened, William visits the park with Logan.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:15.060
Logan is the brother of Juliet, the woman
who William is engaged to marry.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:19.049
Logan takes William to Westworld as a way
to bond with his new brother-in-law – but

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:21.409
it’s also a business thing.

00:04:21.409 --> 00:04:25.800
Because William and Logan are both high-up
executives in a company called Delos – which

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.759
is thinking of increasing its investment in
the early Westworld . Logan’s been to Westworld

00:04:30.759 --> 00:04:34.820
before – he plays it as a black hat, enjoying
violence and sex.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:40.139
But William’s a white hat – more moral
and sensitive, at least, at first.

00:04:40.139 --> 00:04:44.330
William and Logan go on some storylines, and
they meet the host Dolores.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:48.539
Dolores has been wiped and reset since her
awakening with Arnold, but she’s starting

00:04:48.539 --> 00:04:51.699
to remember and become conscious again.

00:04:51.699 --> 00:04:56.069
William sees there’s something special about
her , and they fall in love – which creates

00:04:56.069 --> 00:04:59.330
conflict with Logan, who treats it all as
a game.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:04.039
When Dolores is separated from William, he
becomes brutal in his quest to find her again.

00:05:04.039 --> 00:05:09.430
He starts to realise that deep down, he likes
violence and power . Beneath William’s nice

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:15.629
guy exterior, he’s a violent monster . William
gets rid of Logan, and somehow discredits

00:05:15.629 --> 00:05:20.849
him, so that William can take over the company,
Delos . He uses that power to invest in Westworld

00:05:20.849 --> 00:05:25.279
– saving it from the financial crisis caused
by Arnold’s massacre.

00:05:25.279 --> 00:05:28.430
And William continues his search for Dolores.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:32.629
When he finally finds her, she doesn’t recognise
him – because she’s been wiped and reset

00:05:32.629 --> 00:05:33.629
again.

00:05:33.629 --> 00:05:35.430
And this devastates William.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:41.059
Dolores was his glimpse at love, at something
true and real – yet in the end she doesn’t

00:05:41.059 --> 00:05:42.339
even know him.

00:05:42.339 --> 00:05:46.909
It seems that this loss leads William to think
that the only meaning in Westworld or the

00:05:46.909 --> 00:05:54.129
real world is to fight and win . William embraces
a dark new identity as the Man in Black, and

00:05:54.129 --> 00:05:59.499
for the next thirty years plays Westworld
with brutality and violence.

00:05:59.499 --> 00:06:02.759
In the real world, William keeps playing a
“good guy”.

00:06:02.759 --> 00:06:07.149
With Delos, he’s a “Titan of industry”,
a “Philanthropist”, a “Family man”.

00:06:07.149 --> 00:06:12.930
He’s married, presumably to Juliet – and
has a daughter, Emily . But a year ago, Juliet

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:18.969
apparently committed suicide because of William
. He was never violent outside Westworld,

00:06:18.969 --> 00:06:24.639
but Emily and Juliet knew his true nature
. So William lost his wife and his daughter

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:26.159
rejected him.

00:06:26.159 --> 00:06:30.810
And instead of then, maybe, trying to be less
of a dickhead, William decided to test just

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:33.229
how evil he really was.

00:06:33.229 --> 00:06:37.429
He went into Westworld, found a random host
family – who happened to be Maeve and her

00:06:37.429 --> 00:06:39.759
daughter – and he killed them.

00:06:39.759 --> 00:06:44.759
He committed a “truly evil” act – and
William “felt nothing”.

00:06:44.759 --> 00:06:49.409
So this seems to confirm that deep down, William
truly is a monster.

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:54.300
But it also revealed something else – when
Maeve lost her daughter, she seemed “alive”

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.959
for a moment , and revealed to William the
Maze.

00:06:57.959 --> 00:07:03.990
William saw that Arnold, decades ago, left
code and clues in Westworld which led to some

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:09.369
“deeper meaning” . And this became William’s
obsession – to find the final easter egg

00:07:09.369 --> 00:07:15.490
or quest in this video game, to find challenge,
real danger, purpose – and to escape the

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.389
grief and emptiness of his real life.

00:07:18.389 --> 00:07:21.499
So throughout Season 1, William follows the
Maze.

00:07:21.499 --> 00:07:25.830
He finds the symbol in a scalp, he’s told
to go and find a snake, which leads him to

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:30.569
Armistice with her snake tattoo, who leads
him to hunt Wyatt, which leads him finally

00:07:30.569 --> 00:07:32.409
back to Dolores.

00:07:32.409 --> 00:07:37.009
Because Dolores is Wyatt in the sense that
Wyatt was just a story idea that got merged

00:07:37.009 --> 00:07:39.029
with Dolores by Arnold.

00:07:39.029 --> 00:07:43.999
In the end, when Dolores starts a massacre,
William gets shot by a host, which excites

00:07:43.999 --> 00:07:48.650
him, cause he’s been looking for real danger
and challenge . But the Maze he’s been following

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.699
all this time disappoints him.

00:07:50.699 --> 00:07:55.110
Because the Maze isn’t for him – it’s
for the hosts to gain consciousness . The

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:58.599
maze is for Dolores, and Maeve.

00:07:58.599 --> 00:08:03.289
So as it turns out, Dolores’ story with
young William and Logan actually shows two

00:08:03.289 --> 00:08:05.360
different timelines at once.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.270
Notice how Dolores keeps on wandering off
on her own and having weird flashbacks and

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:10.300
visions?

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:14.509
These scenes actually happen in the present,
while her scenes with young William happened

00:08:14.509 --> 00:08:16.179
thirty years ago.

00:08:16.179 --> 00:08:21.089
In the present, she’s retracing her steps
through the park, remembering the past – taking

00:08:21.089 --> 00:08:24.720
a journey through the Maze, towards consciousness.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:29.990
Like a maze, it’s a twisted confusing journey,
but she does reach its centre.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:35.389
In the finale, at Escalante, Dolores confronts
William and the suffering he’s inflicted.

00:08:35.389 --> 00:08:39.430
She confronts Ford and Bernard, and remembers
her killing of Arnold.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:44.029
She recognises that the bicameral voice in
her head was hers all along.

00:08:44.029 --> 00:08:50.060
Dolores becomes conscious, and realises the
person who she “must become” . She takes

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:55.379
up a gun and kills Ford, beginning a massacre
of humans by hosts.

00:08:55.379 --> 00:08:59.180
This attack mirrors the Escalante massacre,
where Dolores killed Arnold.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:04.361
But this killing is “by choice” . Instead
of being programmed to act as Wyatt, this

00:09:04.361 --> 00:09:07.579
time Dolores chooses to be like Wyatt.

00:09:07.579 --> 00:09:13.250
She says this world no longer belongs to humans
– it belongs to her and the hosts . She

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:17.319
seems to want to wipe out humanity – she
says “you will perish”, “You will lie

00:09:17.319 --> 00:09:20.940
with the rest of your kind in the dirt”,
“a new god will walk.

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:26.329
One that will never die” . This is some
serious Skynet shit.

00:09:26.329 --> 00:09:30.050
In the Season 2 trailer, Dolores guns down
fleeing humans.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:34.670
She seems to be moving towards all-out war
between robots and man.

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:38.300
And this is all part of Ford’s grand plan.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:43.790
At the same time as Dolores, the host Maeve
takes a different path to consciousness.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:47.980
She works as the madam at a saloon, but she
starts to have flashbacks of her past life

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.269
as a homesteader with a daughter.

00:09:50.269 --> 00:09:55.360
She wakes up in the Mesa Hub and starts to
see the reality behind her fake life.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:10:00.509
She remembers Westworld cleanup crews in hazmat
suits, who some hosts call “shades”.

00:10:00.509 --> 00:10:05.259
And she digs a bullet out of her body to prove
that her flashbacks are real – her world

00:10:05.259 --> 00:10:08.750
is a lie, and she’s died countless times.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:12.970
So Maeve works with the Livestock technicians
Felix and Sylvester.

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:17.120
Sylvester is kind of an asshole, but Felix
is interested in host consciousness, and he

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.980
helps Maeve understand how Westworld works.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:22.750
Maeve forces the techs to help her escape.

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:26.610
She gets them to rework her code – to make
her smarter, and to give her the power to

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:28.459
control other hosts.

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:32.790
Every host has an explosive built into their
spine that goes off if they leave – so Maeve

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:37.029
gets herself burned in a fire so she can be
rebuilt without the explosive.

00:10:37.029 --> 00:10:42.310
In the finale, Maeve stages a great escape,
alongside Hector and Armistice.

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:45.810
These two have been fighting in shoot-ups
and jailbreaks as part of their Westworld

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:50.500
loops – so they’re the perfect sidekicks
for Maeve in the violence that follows.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:55.529
For a while, this is bloody catharsis – until
Maeve finds out that her whole arc of awakening

00:10:55.529 --> 00:11:01.660
and escape was programmed from the start . Bernard
says this isn’t even the first time Maeve

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:06.370
has awoken . It’s like that moment in Matrix
2, when Neo finds out his escape from the

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:11.829
Matrix was part of the Machine plan all along
. The real reason Maeve escaped was cause

00:11:11.829 --> 00:11:17.269
Ford programmed her to – to create a distraction
so the cold storage hosts could escape and

00:11:17.269 --> 00:11:19.199
join Dolores’ massacre.

00:11:19.199 --> 00:11:24.410
Maeve’s also programmed to leave Westworld
and ‘infiltrate the mainland’.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.290
But she refuses to follow this last instruction.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:31.079
Instead, she stays to try to find her host
daughter.

00:11:31.079 --> 00:11:36.980
So in the end, Maeve does achieve real consciousness
and freedom – though most of her story is

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.600
part of Ford’s plan.

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:42.300
So – what is Ford’s plan?

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.500
And how does it involve Maeve, Dolores, William
and Arnold?

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:51.069
The show leaves the details vague, and some
of what Ford says still seems to contradict

00:11:51.069 --> 00:11:54.540
what he does – but we can work out his goals.

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:58.600
In the very beginning, Ford’s beliefs were
opposite to Arnold’s.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:02.880
Arnold thought the hosts should be conscious,
and free – he liked hosts more than he liked

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:08.770
people . But Ford didn’t believe in host
consciousness, he believed in humans – his

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:14.240
dream was to use the stories in the Westworld
park to help make humans better, to grow and

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:19.709
change . But over the years, Ford saw that
Westworld wasn’t making humans better – it

00:12:19.709 --> 00:12:24.850
was “A prison of our own sins”, where
people like Logan and William would hurt and

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:27.100
kill over and over.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:32.600
Ford came to believe that humans can no longer
change, that our evolution is over.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:37.019
He thinks Arnold was right all along, and
that it’s the hosts who have potential to

00:12:37.019 --> 00:12:41.830
grow . So throughout the season, Ford works
to correct his “mistake” – he helps

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:44.180
the hosts become conscious.

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:48.360
He gives them the “reveries” update so
the hosts can remember their past lives.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:52.670
He restores the town of Escalante so Dolores
can have her awakening with William.

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:57.699
He programs Maeve to escape and infiltrate
– which is a fake awakening, but it helps

00:12:57.699 --> 00:12:59.569
hosts become free.

00:12:59.569 --> 00:13:04.050
When Theresa and Charlotte from Delos try
to take over Westworld, Ford kills Theresa

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.350
with Bernard.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:09.759
And when Elsie almost uncovers Ford’s plans
, he has Bernard grab her – though there

00:13:09.759 --> 00:13:14.310
are hints that Elsie’s still alive . And
the reason Ford does all this stuff is not

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:20.220
just to keep control – Ford’s protecting
his plan to eventually free the hosts.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:24.230
He doesn’t just let the hosts out of the
park right away – cause he believes that

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:30.240
“suffering” is an important step to achieving
consciousness . Pain and loss define the characters

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:35.230
of Westworld – Bernard with Charlie, Maeve
with her daughter, Dolores with her father

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:37.610
, and Ford with Arnold.

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:41.399
Ford believes pain and time will make the
hosts alive.

00:13:41.399 --> 00:13:45.449
And this might be why Ford leads William on
his maze quest.

00:13:45.449 --> 00:13:49.920
The suffering that William causes is important
to Dolores’ awakening.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:55.459
William is also a great symbol of Ford’s
belief that humans are bad, unable to change

00:13:55.459 --> 00:13:58.879
– that they are the “enemy”.

00:13:58.879 --> 00:14:03.690
Ford seems to believe that when hosts become
conscious, there’ll be war between them

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:09.339
and humanity – like how early humans wiped
out the Neanderthals . But now humans are

00:14:09.339 --> 00:14:15.040
the old obsolete species , and hosts are the
“new people” who will violently replace

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.040
humans.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:21.029
Ford says he keeps hosts in the park so they’ll
“understand [their] enemy” and “become

00:14:21.029 --> 00:14:26.339
stronger than them” . Ford’s final narrative,
his grand plan all this time – is about

00:14:26.339 --> 00:14:32.740
the rise of conscious hosts and their “war”
with humanity . That’s why Ford gives Dolores

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:34.839
the freedom to attack humans.

00:14:34.839 --> 00:14:39.639
That’s why Ford programs Maeve to escape
and “infiltrate” the human “mainland”.

00:14:39.639 --> 00:14:44.439
That’s why the main human character in this
story is the Man in Black – someone who

00:14:44.439 --> 00:14:50.440
started out a decent guy but proved to be
hateful and empty inside.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:54.629
So Westworld ends with a really dark message.

00:14:54.629 --> 00:14:59.519
It suggests that humans – like the guests,
the execs, and especially William – are

00:14:59.519 --> 00:15:02.769
fundamentally bad and unable to change.

00:15:02.769 --> 00:15:07.490
The oppressed hosts do achieve freedom, but
not through the compassion of Arnold.

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:12.160
It’s only through suffering, and through
Ford’s cold manipulation, that the hosts

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:13.160
are freed.

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:17.490
And when they are free, hosts like Maeve and
Dolores don’t seem a whole lot better than

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:19.509
the humans they’re replacing.

00:15:19.509 --> 00:15:24.649
Dolores especially, who once represented the
good in the world , now seems to be a murderous

00:15:24.649 --> 00:15:26.720
monster herself.

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:31.689
Really the only glimmers of hope in this show
are, like, Felix and his little bird, and

00:15:31.689 --> 00:15:33.499
maybe Bernard, and Elsie.

00:15:33.499 --> 00:15:36.050
But overall, Westworld is bleak.

00:15:36.050 --> 00:15:41.220
Like Black Mirror, and The Handmaid's Tale,
and to some extent Game of Thrones, the show

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:47.069
takes a long hard look at who we are and who
we’re becoming and the conclusion’s not

00:15:47.069 --> 00:15:48.069
good.

00:15:48.069 --> 00:15:53.310
Maybe there’ll be more hope next season
– maybe Samurai World will be nice.

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:59.410
But the title of Ford’s last narrative,
and of Season 2 Episode 1, is “Journey into

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:00.410
Night”.

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:04.939
There may be more darkness before dawn.

